# Build context for the container image.
#
# This file must exist. Without it gcloud derives its rules from .gitignore,
# which is not shipped -- so the whole working directory, including anything
# you created next to this package, is uploaded to your Cloud Build staging
# bucket and kept there indefinitely.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
__pycache__
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
# Credentials and local configuration. These must never reach a build context.
.env
.env.*
*-key.json
*_key.json
*.pem
manifest.json
# `runtime` is deliberately NOT ignored: the Dockerfile stages it into the
# package so /v1/mcps/{id}/bundle.zip can ship the code your MCP actually runs.
